{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Image Tampering Evidence.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Image Tampering Evidence.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"image tampering evidence image tampering evidence","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Image Tampering Evidence.md","fileName":"Image Tampering Evidence.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Image Tampering Evidence","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Image Authenticity and Forensic Reasoning]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Image Authenticity and Forensic Reasoning","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Image Tampering Evidence.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Image Tampering Evidence.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"image tampering evidence image tampering evidence","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Image Tampering Evidence.md","fileName":"Image Tampering Evidence.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Image Tampering Evidence","heading":"Image Tampering Evidence","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Image tampering evidence is an observable inconsistency that an expected capture or encoding process does not explain. Examples include incompatible shadows, a locally missing sensor pattern, a second compression history, duplicated image structure, or metadata that conflicts with the visible scene.\n\nSome findings directly localize an edit, while others show only that a file was resaved or passed through unexpected software. The conclusion should preserve that distinction: evidence of post-processing is not automatically evidence that the depicted event was fabricated.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Image Authenticity and Forensic Reasoning","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Image Tamperi